estion iOS Listening Ways to listen\nL13: ## Listen in the app\nL14: \nL15:   * Oct 13, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Listen in the app\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: listen-in-the-app\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: You can listen to free or purchased titles on the Audible app anytime — no membership required. All you need is an Amazon account to get started. The Audible app gives you full control over your listening experience with customizable player settings, narration speed, timers, and more.\nL29: Note: The Audible app is available for iOS and Android devices. For a full list of supported devices, visit 【1†Devices compatible with Audible】.\nL30: \nL31: In this article:\nL32: \nL33:   * 【2†How do I install the app?】\nL34:   * 【3†How do I listen to titles in the app?】\nL35:   * 【4†How do I resume playback in the Audible app?】\nL36:   * 【5†How do I sync my listening across devices?】\nL37:   * 【6†Where do I find my player settings?】\nL38:   * 【7†What features can I use in the player?】\nL39:   * 【8†Can't listen or having playback issues?】\nL40: ## How do I install the app?\nL41: \nL42: You can download the Audible app on your iOS mobile devices—including Apple Watch, Android device, Galaxy device, and Fire TV.\nL43: \nL44: On my iOS Device\nL45: \nL46:   1. Open the App Store on your Apple device.\nL47:   2. Search for “Audible.”\nL48:   3. Select Get next to the Audible app.\nL49:   4. Select Install.\nL50: \nL51: On my Apple Watch\nL52: \nL53: Before you begin, you’ll need to make sure your Apple Watch is paired with your iPhone.\nL54:   1. Open the Apple Watch app on your iPhone.\nL55:   2. Select the My Watch tab.\nL56:   3. Scroll down to Available Apps.\nL57:   4. Select the Install button next to the Audible app.\nL58: \nL59: On my Android Device\nL60: \nL61:   1. Open the Google Play store on your device and search for \"Audible.\"\nL62:   2. Select Audible: Audio Entertainment.\nL63:   3. Select Install.\nL64: \nL65: On my Fire TV\nL66: \nL67: You can enjoy Audible on your Fire TV or Fire TV Stick FOS7/FOS8 via the Audible app for Fire TV.\nL68:   1. Search for Audible to bring up the app. You can also use the Voice Control button on your remote and search by saying \"Audible.\"\nL69:   2. Navigate to Apps.\nL70:   3. Find the Audible app.\nL71:   4. Select Get.\nL72: ## How do I listen to titles in the app?\nL73: \nL74:   1. Open the Audible app and sign in with your Amazon account.\nL75:   2. Go to your Library.\nL76:   3. Select a title to play.\nL77: \nL78: Note: If your Library appears empty or you can't find a title, visit 【9†Missing title issues】 for troubleshooting steps.\nL79: ## How do I resume playback in the Audible app?\nL80: \nL81: If you've already started a title, you can select Play to resume listening on the Audible mini player. You can also resume listening from your lock screen controls without opening the app.\nL82: ## How do I sync my listening across devices?\nL83: \nL84: The Audible app will automatically sync your listening position across devices. To manage this setting:\nL85: \nL86:   1. Go to your Profile.\nL87:   2. Select the Settings gear icon.\nL88:   3. Select Player.\nL89:   4. Toggle the Sync listening position slider on or off.\nL90: \nL91: Troubleshooting sync issues: If your listening position is not syncing correctly, toggle the Sync listening position slider off, then on again to reset the connection.\nL92: ## Where do I find my player settings?\nL93: \nL94: Note: Player settings are available only in the Audible app for iOS and Android.\nL95: \nL96: From the player\nL97: \nL98:   1. Open the player.\nL99:   2. Select the 3-dot More menu at the top of the screen.\nL100:   3. Select Player settings.\nL101: \nL102: From your Profile\nL103: \nL104:   1. Go to your Profile.\nL105:   2. Select the Settings gear icon.\nL106:   3. Select Player.\nL107: \nL108: You can adjust or turn on or off the following settings:\nL109:   * Player customization.\nL110:   * Progress bar per chapter or for the whole title.\nL111:   * How many seconds you skip forward or back.\nL112:   * How you want to see time displayed in the mini player while listening.\nL113:   * Shake to extend for your timer.\nL114:   * Auto-lock for your screen.\nL115:   * Automatic Car Mode.\nL116:   * Sync listening position.\nL117:   * Continuous listening (affects automatic listening samples, podcast episodes, and the play queue).\nL118: ## What features can I use in the player?\nL119: \nL120: The Audible player gives you access to several features while listening like:\nL121: \nL122:   1. 【10†Browse chapters or podcast episodes】.\nL123:   2. 【11†View your listening log】\nL124:   3. 【12†Change the narration speed】\nL125:   4. 【13†Use timer】.\nL126:   5. 【14†Manage your auto-play settings】.\nL127:   6. 【15†Create a listening reminder】\nL128: ## Can't listen or having playback issues?\nL129: \nL130: If you're having trouble playing a title in the app, visit 【16†Audio quality issues】 for detailed troubleshooting steps by device type, including how to update the app, re-download titles, change download quality, and more.\nL131: \nL132: Did this answer your question?\nL133: \nL134: 【17†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL135: \nL136: \nL137: \nL138: 【18†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL139: \nL140:  Back to top\nL141: \nL142: 【19†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL143: \nL144: 【20†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL145: ## Need more assistance?\nL146: \nL147: 【21†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL148: \nL149: \nL150: \nL151: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL152: \nL153: \nL154: \nL155: Worst\nL156: \nL157: 1\nL158: \nL159: 2\nL160: \nL161: 3\nL162: \nL163: 4\nL164: \nL165: 5\nL166: \nL167: 6\nL168: \nL169: 7\nL170: \nL171: Best\nL172: \nL173: \nL174: \nL175: Region\nL176: \nL177: United States\nL178: \nL179: Language\nL180: \nL181: English\nL182: \nL183: Loading\nL184: \nL185: Listen in the app 【22†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nManage your Library (https://help.audible.com/s/article/manage-your-library)\nciteturn757view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://help.audible.com/s/article/manage-your-library\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 261\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Android Downloads iOS Library Library issues+3\nL13: ## Manage your Library\nL14: \nL15:   * Sep 9, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Manage your Library\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: manage-your-library\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: Your Library is the place to go when you'd like to listen to any audiobook you've added or purchased, or when you want to catch up on a podcast you chose to follow. From here, you can easily keep track of which titles you've started and have yet to listen to. You can also view and manage your 【1†Wish List】 and 【2†Lists】 from your desktop and in-app Library.\nL29: \nL30: In this article:\nL31:   * 【3†How can I access my Library?】\nL32:   * 【4†How can I use my Library?】\nL33:   * 【5†How do I add audiobooks to my Library?】\nL34:   * 【6†How do I remove audiobooks from my Library?】\nL35:   * 【7†How do I delete a downloaded audiobook from my device?】\nL36:   * 【8†How do I delete audiobooks from my Library?】\nL37:   * 【9†How do I refresh my app Library?】\nL38:   * 【10†How can I remove podcasts from my Library?】\nL39: ## How can I access my Library?\nL40: \nL41: In the app\nL42: \nL43:   1. Open the Audible app and sign in.\nL44:   2. Select Library in the bottom navigation.\nL45: \nL46: On mobile web\nL47: \nL48:   1. Go to the Audible site and sign in.\nL49:   2. Select the main menu.\nL50:   3. Select Library.\nL51: \nL52: On desktop\nL53: \nL54:   1. Go to the Audible site and sign in.\nL55:   2. Select Library in the site navigation.\nL56: ## How can I use my Library?\nL57: \nL58: In the app\nL59: \nL60: There are several ways you can view and sort titles in your in-app Library. At the very top of the screen, you'll find your main sections—Audiobooks, Podcasts, Wish List, Lists, Authors, Series, and Genres. Simply swipe left on the screen to view them all.\nL61: \nL62: Your in-app Library also features filters, which allow you to see all of your titles at once or only those that are Not started, In progress, Downloaded, and Finished.\nL63: ### Use the In your library filter in catalog search\nL64: \nL65: When searching in the Audible app, you can use the In your library filter to narrow search results to titles in your Library only.\nL66: \nL67:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL68:   2. Search for the title you are looking for.\nL69:   3. Select In your library from the suggestions that appear to find titles you own.\nL70: \nL71: Use this option to find titles that you own and are no longer available in the Audible catalog.\nL72: \nL73: On desktop\nL74: There are several ways you can view and sort titles in your Library on desktop and mobile web. At the very top of the page, you'll find your main sections—All, Audiobooks, Podcasts, Wish List, Collections, and Authors.\nL75: \nL76: Your web Library also features filters, which allow you to see all of your titles at once or only those that are Finished and Unfinished.\nL77: ## How do I add audiobooks to my Library?\nL78: \nL79: Titles you purchase with a credit or credit card will automatically show up in your Library, and you can easily add included titles via the site or app.\nL80: \nL81: In the app\nL82: \nL83:   1. Open the Audible app and sign in.\nL84:   2. Search for the title you're interested in adding to your Library.\nL85:   3. Select the title to go to its detail page.\nL86:   4. Select Add to Library.\nL87: \nL88: On desktop\nL89:   1. Go to the Audible site and sign in.\nL90:   2. Go to 'Find your next great listen'\nL91:   3. Select the title and go to its detail page.\nL92:   4. Select Add to Library.\nL93: \nL94: From the search results on desktop\nL95: \nL96:   1. Go to 'Find your next great listen'\nL97:   2. Search for the title you want\nL98:   3. On the search results, select Add to Library next to the title you want.\nL99: \nL100: From the Wish List on desktop\nL101: \nL102:   1. Go to Wish list\nL103:   2. Locate the title you want\nL104:   3. Select Add to Library next to the title.\nL105: \nL106: On Mobile\nL107:   1. Search for the title you want\nL108:   2. Select the title you want\nL109:   3. Select Add to Library.\nL110: \nL111: From the Wish List on Mobile\nL112: \nL113:   1. Select the main menu\nL114:   2. Select Wish list\nL115:   3. Select the title you want\nL116:   4. Select Add to Library.\nL117: ## How do I remove audiobooks from my Library?\nL118: \nL119: On desktop\nL120: \nL121:   1. Go to the Audible Site\nL122:   2. Select to Library\nL123:   3. Select the title you want  to remove\nL124:   4. Select Remove\nL125: \nL126: In the app\nL127: \nL128: Remove a specific title\nL129: \nL130:   1. Go to your Library.\nL131:   2. Find the title you'd like to remove.\nL132:   3. Select the 3-dot More menu.\nL133:   4. Select Remove from Library.\nL134: \nL135: Remove multiple titles\nL136:   1. Go to your Library.\nL137:   2. Select Select.\nL138:   3. Pick the titles you'd like to remove by selecting the boxes.\nL139:   4. Select Remove from Library.\nL140: \nL141: Note: Removing titles from your Library doesn't permanently delete them. The titles you purchase with a credit or credit card are yours to keep.\nL142: ## How do I delete a downloaded audiobook from my device?\nL143: \nL144: If you'd like to free up space on your device without removing a title from your Library, you can delete the download file.\nL145: \nL146: In the app\nL147: \nL148:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL149:   2. Select Library.\nL150:   3. Find the title you want to remove from your device.\nL151:   4. Select the 3-dot More menu.\nL152:   5. Select Remove download.\nL153: \nL154: Delete multiple downloaded titles:\nL155:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL156:   2. Select Library\nL157:   3. Choose Select.\nL158:   4. Pick the titles you would like to delete by selecting the boxes\nL159:   5. Select Remove Download.\nL160: \nL161: Note: Removing a download from your device does not remove the title from your Library. You can re-download it at any time.\nL162: ## How do I delete audiobooks from my Library?\nL163: \nL164: You can only permanently delete audiobooks through the Amazon website or by contacting Customer Support.\nL165: \nL166:   1. Go to 【11†Manage Your Content and Devices†www.amazon.com】 on Amazon.\nL167:   2. Filter by Content.\nL168:   3. Choose the audiobook you want to delete and select Delete.\nL169:   4. Confirm by selecting Yes, delete permanently.\nL170: \nL171: Note: Once you permanently delete titles from your account, you won't be able to access them again in your Library or on any device.\nL172: ## How do I refresh my app Library?\nL173: \nL174: To ensure that your app Library refreshes, you must have the latest version of the app installed on your device. To learn how, go to App 【12†Keeps Crashing】.\nL175: \nL176: To refresh the app Library, please follow these steps:\nL177: \nL178: In the app\nL179: \nL180:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL181:   2. Select Profile.\nL182:   3. Select the Settings gear.\nL183:   4. Select Library.\nL184:   5. Select Refresh Library.\nL185: Note: If you're using an older device that doesn't support the latest version of the app, you can continue to listen to all of your audiobooks on another compatible device or in the Audible Cloud Player.\nL186: ## How can I remove podcasts from my Library?\nL187: \nL188: To remove a podcast from your Library, follow these steps:\nL189: \nL190: Using the 3-dot menu:\nL191: \nL192:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL193:   2. Select Library.\nL194:   3. Select Podcasts.\nL195:   4. Select the 3-dot menu of the podcast you want to remove.\nL196:   5. Select Unfollow.\nL197: \nL198: Using select and hold:\nL199: \nL200:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL201:   2. Select Library.\nL202:   3. Select Podcasts.\nL203:   4. Tap and hold the podcast you want to remove.\nL204:   5. Select Unfollow.\nL205: The podcast has been removed and will no longer show in your Library.\nL206: \nL207: Did this answer your question?\nL208: \nL209: 【13†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL210: \nL211: \nL212: \nL213: 【14†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL214: \nL215:  Back to top\nL216: \nL217: 【15†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL218: \nL219: 【16†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL220: ## Need more assistance?\nL221: \nL222: 【17†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL223: \nL224: \nL225: \nL226: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL227: \nL228: \nL229: \nL230: Worst\nL231: \nL232: 1\nL233: \nL234: 2\nL235: \nL236: 3\nL237: \nL238: 4\nL239: \nL240: 5\nL241: \nL242: 6\nL243: \nL244: 7\nL245: \nL246: Best\nL247: \nL248: \nL249: \nL250: Region\nL251: \nL252: United States\nL253: \nL254: Language\nL255: \nL256: English\nL257: \nL258: Loading\nL259: \nL260: Manage your Library 【18†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n"
